## Case Priority and Instruction Usage
The retrieved cases are the primary basis of the placement prediction. Give greater weight to earlier cases, then compare their situations with the current rally before making the decision.

First prioritize cases that best match the incoming shuttle, player and opponent positions, movement and reachability, prior rally actions, score pressure, and the current Twin semantic query. Predict landing and recovery behavior from the nearest compatible cases for the locked Stage-1 shot type.

Treat the tactical imitation instruction as weak auxiliary information. Use it only to rerank otherwise similarly relevant cases. Keep the prediction case-driven: the instruction must not make a less compatible case more important than a clearly more compatible case.

Do not construct a landing area, recovery area, or coordinate directly from the instruction. Every selected area and coordinate bias must be supported by the nearest compatible cases.

If the instruction conflicts with the nearest compatible cases, ignore the instruction and follow the cases.

